<!--Post: 13429--><!--Time: 1115265230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13429"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 8:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Poem #1 called &#34;Black Friday&#34; <BR>  <BR>Just a quick glance and I knew all was lost.  <BR>I saw in real life...now a on going mind view, the black and white, were now my new boss. <BR>I saw my life as I know quickly fade away.  <BR>I saw my love ones, in mind and thoughts that I would never be able to touch, hold, communicate closely with and kiss with care will now be at bay. <BR>I saw the Black Side of me, was now caught and others would not suffer from my lots, <BR>But then it dawn on me, it was not as I thought. <BR>Yes the other in me will cause no suffering. <BR>The living remained, the Mother, Brother, Sisters, Children, Close Friends and wife will suffer. <BR>Ands the real me of blood, flesh and mind will suffer. <BR>  <BR>&#40;signed &#34;The Suspect&#34; 4-2005&#41; <BR>  <BR>Poem #2 called &#34;Tis&#39; Spring out there&#34; <BR> <BR>Oh, to walk among the new Season, <BR>-to heard a robin voice, <BR>-to see a dandelion bright, <BR>-to watch a butterfly flight, <BR>-to smell a simple flower bud, <BR>Oh Spring these are the many reasons. <BR> <BR>&#40;signed&#41; Dennis L. Rader 4-16-2005 <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13429-->
<!--Post: 13431--><!--Time: 1115267349-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13431"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 9:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Poem #3 &#34;Tis&#39; hell in here&#34; <BR> <BR>Oh, to walk in the new prison, <BR>-to hear the gaurds voice yell <BR>-&#34;Off with the lights.&#34; <BR>-to see a prison shank fight, <BR>-to smell like my cellmates sweat, <BR>Oh Spring and 159 more seasons to go. <BR> <BR>&#40;signed&#41; Johno. 5-4-2005<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13431-->
<!--Post: 13432--><!--Time: 1115267798-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13432"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 9:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Man. I&#39;m about to say the dumbest thing I&#39;ve ever written here. <BR> <BR>Those suck. <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s a <a href="http://blogcritics.org/archives/2005/05/05/004113.php">blogcritics entry</a> I did about &#39;em.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13432-->
<!--Post: 13433--><!--Time: 1115268099-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13433"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 9:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Poem #4 &#34;&#39;Tis my Butt doth hurt!&#34; <BR> <BR>Oh to sleep in my bunk, <BR>- to hear the words &#34;fishy-fish&#34; <BR>- to befriend inmates who like to &#34;swish&#34; <BR>- to have my cellmate admire &#34;junk in my trunk&#34; <BR>- to sleep with my back against the wall <BR>Oh for two of us this bunk is just way too small. <BR> <BR>&#40;signed&#41; Steve. 5-5-5 <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13433-->
<!--Post: 13435--><!--Time: 1115273252-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13435"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Victor<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victor<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 11:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Denny Poem #5: <BR> <BR>&#34;There once was a man from Nantuckett, <BR>Who&#39;s...&#34; <BR> <BR>[P.S. I just changed my Username from &#34;Vscantu&#34; to &#34;Victor&#34;. Thanks to Ed for his help.]<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13435-->
<!--Post: 13437--><!--Time: 1115290727-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13437"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 3:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To all literalists, only Poem #1 and Poem #2 are real. The other poems are mere fakes, although much better than the originals. Thanks, guys. Steve, loved your blog entry on the poems. Victor, congrats on your new username! hagd <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13437-->
<!--Post: 13440--><!--Time: 1115302563-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13440"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 7:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was not able to watch the show on KAKE...did he mail these poems directly to them, or was this from someone writing to dogbreath?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13440-->
<!--Post: 13447--><!--Time: 1115313483-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13447"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Miss<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Miss<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 10:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, they definitely have that BTK, non-native English speaker ring to them, don&#39;t they? <BR> <BR>So do you think that he&#39;s just sloppy, or do you think that when he speaks he&#39;s always using the wrong verb tenses too? <BR> <BR>&#34;To heard a robin...&#34; <BR>It seems like he makes this same weird mistake in all his written communications.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13447-->
<!--Post: 13448--><!--Time: 1115314113-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13448"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 10:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I personally think it&#39;s dyslexia.  But what the hell do I know.  Remember when he made the phone call when he murdered Nancy... <BR>&#34;You will find a home i cide&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13448-->
<!--Post: 13472--><!--Time: 1115356061-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13472"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 10:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The &#34;other&#34; in me. Hmmmm? Interesting way to put the blame on his alter-ego. He needs to stop writing poetry. That is for sure.  &#34;It was not as I thought&#34; No, He thought he would get away with it. Someone must have told him, He needed to get a personality real fast. Can you imagine Rader stoping to smell flowers? Give me a break.  Someone please take away his pen and paper.  Funny, it&#39;s a far cry from the poetry he was writing when he was out here.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13472-->
<!--Post: 13486--><!--Time: 1115388854-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13486"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 7:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He is so transparent, the happy spring flower smellin rader signed his poem Dennis L rader <BR> <BR>The dark black friday bubbu luvr signed his the suspect. <BR> <BR>Everything we have heard about him so far, are complete opposites. He heard about this dual personality thing years ago, and has read all the books on them, and is trying his darndest to convince everyone. Remember the headline <BR> <BR>&#34;Police say Btk&#39;s writing syle has changed&#34; <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13486-->
<!--Post: 13489--><!--Time: 1115394810-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13489"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 8:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->GO Itty - Emb - doesn&#39;t the demon @&#42;&#42; just make you want to vomit? <BR>He is playing his cards. <BR>His research was done. <BR>He thinks he is soooooooooo smart... <BR>I hope he kept a journal of more poemsy poems...the @&#42;&#42; <BR>Just when was it that he did stop and smell any flowers in his life. <BR>...after he snuffed the life out of victim... <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13489-->
<!--Post: 13495--><!--Time: 1115397577-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13495"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 9:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is the link to the &#34;Black Friday&#34; poem: <a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1542562.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1542562.html</a> <BR> <BR>Here is the link to &#34;Tis&#39; Spring out there&#34;: <a href="http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1546682.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1546682.html</a> <BR> <BR>Each link has a news article about the poem and its own video. <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13495-->
<!--Post: 13496--><!--Time: 1115397778-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13496"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is the poem from the letter that KSN has: <BR> <BR>&#34;Peas in the Pod.&#34; <BR> <BR>     It reads: <BR> <BR>     The green color Pods at First were long and hollow. <BR> <BR>     They had grown from Mother Earth, anti-society, into a wild vine. <BR> <BR>     The vine with Pods, long and curling upward, had many follows; <BR> <BR>     How each Pod has a unique Pea, that together walks a fine line.&#34; <BR> <BR>     At the end of the poem, Dennis Rader writes his initials, the date, and &#34;Day 54&#34;. <BR> <BR>See the news article here: <a href="http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/7727565.html" target=_top>http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/7727565.html</a> <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13496-->
<!--Post: 13499--><!--Time: 1115401381-->
